{'symbol': 'ACN', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Accenture Assists Navantia in Design, Development and Implementation of Advanced Technologies to Improve Shipbuilding', 'text': "Accenture has been selected to assist Navantia with the design, development and implementation of 'Shipyard 4.0,' a new technology platform that leverages digital technologies to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of ship design and construction. The platform will employ capabilities such as digital twins, modelling and simulation, and artificial intelligence (AI) to help Navantia accelerate ship design and development, optimize the construction process, including meeting maximum safety standards, and develop new services across the operational lifetime of its vessels. The first ship to benefit from using the Shipyard 4.0 platform will be the new F-110 frigate, part of a new class of combat vessels for the Spanish Navy. The new platform will help Navantia improve its business management systems throughout a vessel’s entire lifecycle. The rest of Navantia's new projects will follow. Accenture will also work with Navantia over the next three years with the integration of Navantia’s end-to-end business processes, facilitating the interaction with customers and suppliers. The project will involve more than 1,000 engineers, 40 construction and engineering firms, 200 suppliers, four shipyards and all of Navantia’s business lines: Shipbuilding, Systems, Repairs, Propulsion, Life Cycle Support, Wind, and Technology Transfer Program."}{'symbol': 'A', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Akoya Biosciences, Inc. announced that it has received $50 million in funding from Telegraph Hill Partners, Innovatus Capital Partners, LLC, PJC Capital Management LLC, Agilent Technologies, Inc.', 'text': 'Akoya Biosciences, Inc. announced that it has received $50 million in a round of funding led by PJC Capital Management LLC on December 5, 2019. The transaction included participation from new investors Innovatus Capital Partners, LLC and Agilent Technologies, Inc. (NYSE:A) along with returning investor Telegraph Hill Partners. As a part of transaction, Thomas Schnettler of PJC Capital Management LLC will join company board of directors.'}{'symbol': 'ARE', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Alexandria Real Estate Equities, Inc. Declares Quarterly Cash Dividend for the Fourth Quarter of 2019, Payable on January 15, 2020', 'text': 'Alexandria Real Estate Equities, Inc. announced that its Board of Directors declared a quarterly cash dividend of $1.03 per common share for the fourth quarter of 2019. The dividend is payable on January 15, 2020, to shareholders of record on December 31, 2019. The common stock dividend for the year ended December 31, 2019, of $4.00 per common share represents an increase of 27 cents, or 7%, over the year ended December 31, 2018.'}{'symbol': 'ALLE', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Allegion plc Declares Quarterly Dividend, Payable on December 30, 2019', 'text': 'Allegion plc announced that its board of directors declared a quarterly dividend of $0.27 per ordinary share of the company. The dividend is payable on Dec. 30, 2019, to shareholders of record on Dec. 17, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'AMZN', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'U.S. Antitrust Enforcers Have Broadened Scrutiny Of Amazon Beyond Its Retail Operations To Include Its Cloud-Computing Business - Bloomberg Law', 'text': 'Dec 4  - :U.S. ANTITRUST ENFORCERS HAVE BROADENED SCRUTINY OF AMAZON BEYOND ITS RETAIL OPERATIONS TO INCLUDE ITS CLOUD-COMPUTING BUSINESS - BLOOMBERG LAW.'}{'symbol': 'AAL', 'date': '2019-12-05 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'American Airlines To Launch Mobile App Passport Scanning', 'text': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES - TO LAUNCH MOBILE APP PASSPORT SCANNING.AMERICAN AIRLINES - TO OFFER PASSPORT CHIP SCANNING THAT SECURELY TRANSMITS PASSPORT INFORMATION DIRECTLY FROM NFC CHIP EMBEDDED IN PASSPORT.'}{'symbol': 'AEP', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "American Electric Power Announces Lionel L. Nowell, III Not Be Standing for Re-Election as a Director at the Company's 2020", 'text': "On December 3, 2019, Lionel L. Nowell, III notified the Board of Directors of American Electric Power Company, Inc. that he will not be standing for re-election as a director at the Company's 2020 annual meeting of shareholders. Effective January 1, 2020, the Board appointed David J. Anderson as the Chairman of the Audit Committee. Mr. Anderson is currently a member of the Audit Committee. Effective January 1, 2020, the Board also appointed Mr. Art A. Garcia as Chairman of the Finance Committee. Mr. Garcia is currently a member of the Finance Committee."}{'symbol': 'ANSS', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Telma Shortens Path to Market for Frictionless Braking Systems with ANSYS', 'text': "Telma significantly shortened time to market and optimized product development costs using ANSYS for three new series of retarders - braking systems that use electromagnetic induction. With ANSYS, Telma decreased the number of prototypes required for validation from 10 to one over the course of a decade — enabling faster development of retarders that reduce fine-particle emissions associated with braking systems by up to 90% while significantly reducing maintenance costs. Retarders are used in heavy vehicles, mining applications, wind turbines and elevators to dissipate most of the large amounts of energy produced during deceleration. This requires testing and validating the retarders under extreme conditions to ensure the function and safety of the application. With ANSYS, Telma engineers replaced their time-consuming and expensive physical prototyping and testing process with simulation, enabling engineers to better manage the electromagnetical, fluid and structural mechanic phenomena at work. Using ANSYS' high-fidelity multiphysics simulation solutions to model, simulate and validate these virtual prototypes, Telma significantly reduced costs and accelerated time to market."}{'symbol': 'AMAT', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Applied Materials, Inc. Approves Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on March 11, 2020', 'text': 'Applied Materials, Inc. announced that its Board of Directors has approved a quarterly cash dividend of $0.21 per share payable on the company’s common stock. The dividend is payable on March 11, 2020 to shareholders of record as of Feb. 19, 2020.'}{'symbol': 'AJG', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Gallagher Appoints Dave Partington CEO of Canadian Brokerage Operations', 'text': "Gallagher has named Dave Partington CEO of its Canadian retail property/casualty brokerage operations, where he will lead the strategy and culture for continued growth across the country. Partington joined Gallagher in 2012, initially leading the regional offices of Gallagher Heath in the UK. In 2014, he relocated to the US as President of the Small Business Practice for Gallagher's retail P/C brokerage operations. While in the US, he doubled the practice's revenue, created a sales and service infrastructure, led and supported multiple mergers, and enhanced market relationships. Prior to joining Gallagher, Partington held leadership positions with two other large brokerages."}{'symbol': 'AJG', 'date': '2019-12-05 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Arthur J. Gallagher & Acquires Blueleaf Consulting Pty Ltd', 'text': 'ARTHUR J. GALLAGHER & CO. ACQUIRES BLUELEAF CONSULTING PTY LTD..ARTHUR J GALLAGHER & CO - TERMS OF TRANSACTION WERE NOT DISCLOSED..ARTHUR J GALLAGHER & CO - ANNOUNCED ACQUISITION OF NORTH SYDNEY, NEW SOUTH WALES-BASED BLUELEAF CONSULTING PTY LTD.'}{'symbol': 'T', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Barclays Capital Inc. has been added as the Co-Lead Underwriter for AT&T Inc.'s $1.2 billion Fixed-Income Offering.", 'text': "Barclays Capital Inc. has been added as the Co-Lead Underwriter for AT&T Inc.'s $1.2 billion Fixed-Income Offering."}{'symbol': 'BWA', 'date': '2019-12-05 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'BorgWarner Says Start Of Production Of High Voltage Hairpin 146 Motor Planned For Early 2020', 'text': 'BORGWARNER EXPANDS HIGH VOLTAGE HAIRPIN ELECTRIC MOTOR SERIES, INTRODUCES HVH 146.BORGWARNER INC - START OF PRODUCTION OF HIGH VOLTAGE HAIRPIN 146 MOTOR PLANNED FOR EARLY 2020.'}{'symbol': 'BSX', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Boston Scientific Corporation Enters into $700 Million Credit Agreement', 'text': 'On December 5, 2019, Boston Scientific Corporation entered into a $700 million credit agreement by and among the company, as Borrower, the several lenders party thereto, Wells Fargo Bank, National Association, as Syndication Agent, The Bank of Nova Scotia and Wells Fargo Securities, LLC, as Joint Lead Arrangers and Joint Bookrunners, and The Bank of Nova Scotia, as Administrative Agent. The 2019 Credit Agreement provides for a $700 million 364 Day Term Loan, maturing on December 3, 2020. The principal amount of the 2019 Term Loan will bear interest at an annual rate of LIBOR plus a margin of 0.65%. In addition, the Company will pay customary expenses. The 2019 Credit Agreement contains covenants which, among other things, require that the Company maintain a maximum leverage ratio of 3.75x; provided that for the two consecutive fiscal quarters ended immediately following the consummation of a “Qualified Acquisition” (the acquisition on August 19, 2019 of BTG plc, a public company organized under the laws of England and Wales and any other transaction for which the consideration exceeds $1,000,000,000 and for which the Company notifies the Administrative Agent that such transaction is a Qualified Acquisition under the 2019 Credit Agreement), the maximum leverage ratio shall be 4.75x, and shall be decreased to 4.50x, 4.25x, 4.00x, for the next three fiscal quarter-ends after such two fiscal quarter-ends, respectively, and then to 3.75x for each fiscal quarter-end thereafter. The ratio is calculated based on earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization, as adjusted pursuant to the 2019 Credit Agreement. The 2019 Credit Agreement also contains customary events of default, which may result in the acceleration of any outstanding commitments. The company has customary corporate and commercial banking relationships with the lenders, the Syndication Agent and the Administrative Agent and their affiliates.'}{'symbol': 'BMY', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Bristol-Myers Squibb Company Announces Quarterly Dividend, Payable on February 3, 2020; Announces Preference Dividend, Payable on March 2, 2020; Provides Dividend Guidance for the Full Year 2020', 'text': 'The Board of Directors of Bristol-Myers Squibb Company declared an increase of 9.8% in the company’s quarterly dividend, beginning in the first quarter of 2020. The dividend increase will result in a quarterly dividend of forty-five cents ($0.45) per share on the $0.10 par value Common Stock of the corporation. The next quarterly dividend will be payable on February 3, 2020, to stockholders of record at the close of business on January 3, 2020. The directors also declared a quarterly dividend of fifty cents ($0.50) per share on the $2.00 Convertible Preferred Stock of the corporation, payable March 2, 2020 to stockholders of record at the close of business on February 4, 2020. The directors indicated an expected dividend for the full year of 2020 of $1.80 per share on the $0.10 par value Common Stock of the corporation, subject to the normal quarterly review by the Board.'}{'symbol': 'BR', 'date': '2019-12-05 21:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Broadridge Announces Pricing Of $750 Million Senior Notes', 'text': 'BROADRIDGE ANNOUNCES PRICING OF $750 MILLION SENIOR NOTES.BROADRIDGE FINANCIAL SOLUTIONS -  ANNOUNCED IT HAS PRICED $750 MILLION AGGREGATE PRINCIPAL AMOUNT OF 2.900% SENIOR NOTES DUE 2029.'}{'symbol': 'BF-B', 'date': '2019-12-05 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Brown-Forman Reports Q2 Earnings Per Share $0.59', 'text': "BROWN-FORMAN REPORTS FIRST HALF RESULTS; REAFFIRMS FULL YEAR EARNINGS PER SHARE OUTLOOK FOR FISCAL 2020.SEES FY 2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.75 TO $1.85.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.59.Q2 SALES $989 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $974.8 MILLION.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.52 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.RESULTS IMPROVED DURING Q2.REMAIN ON TRACK TO DELIVER ANOTHER YEAR OF MID-SINGLE DIGIT GROWTH IN UNDERLYING NET SALES LED BY JACK DANIEL'S FAMILY OF BRANDS.REAFFIRMED ITS FULL YEAR FISCAL 2020 GUIDANCE FOR UNDERLYING NET SALES GROWTH AND DILUTED EARNINGS PER SHARE.BROWN-FORMAN -DUE TO UNCERTAINTY IN GEOPOLITICAL ENVIRONMENT, MODESTLY REDUCED 2020 UNDERLYING OPERATING INCOME GROWTH FORECAST RANGE BY 1 PERCENTAGE POINT.BROWN-FORMAN SAYS CONTINUE TO INVEST IN CONSUMER MOMENTUM BY ABSORBING MOST TARIFF-RELATED COSTS.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.79, REVENUE VIEW $3.49 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA."}{'symbol': 'CHRW', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'C.H. Robinson Worldwide, Inc. Declares Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on December 31, 2019', 'text': 'C.H. Robinson Worldwide, Inc. announced that its Board of Directors declared an increase to its regular quarterly cash dividend to 51 cents ($0.51) per share from 50 cents ($0.50) per share, payable on December 31, 2019, to shareholders of record on December 16, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'CNC', 'date': '2019-12-05 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Centene And Wellcare Receive State Approvals For Pending Merger From Illinois And New Jersey', 'text': "CENTENE AND WELLCARE RECEIVE STATE APPROVALS FOR PENDING MERGER FROM ILLINOIS AND NEW JERSEY.CENTENE CORP - ALL 27 STATES HAVE PROVIDED APPROVALS OF CENTENE'S CONTROL OF WELLCARE DOMESTIC INSURERS.CENTENE CORP - MERGER REMAINS ON TRACK TO CLOSE BY FIRST HALF OF 2020."}{'symbol': 'CSCO', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Auvik Expands Collaboration with Cisco to Improve Insight into Network Devices', 'text': 'Auvik Networks announced that it is expanding its collaboration with Cisco to give MSPs additional insight into the status of Cisco network devices. An initial integration between Auvik and Cisco, announced in April 2019, used the Cisco Service API to surface warranty and firmware information about Cisco network equipment directly within Auvik. Updates to the API now give Auvik users visibility into whether Cisco network equipment is under a current or expiring support contract, whether theres a more up-to-date software version available, if the device is still eligible to receive critical security updates, and if the device is still available for purchase. With this additional insight, Auvik partners are able to identify obsolete network equipment that presents business and security risks for their clients. The information can be built into an initial network assessment process as well as ongoing client technology roadmaps, opening up new revenue opportunities for Auvik partners. Current Auvik partners can refer to the Auvik Knowledge Base for details on using the Cisco integration. Additional information can also be found on Cisco DevNet, Ciscos developer platform. MSPs who arent yet Auvik partners can request a demo for more information.'}{'symbol': 'CME', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'CME Group Announces Enhancements to NYMEX WTI Houston Crude Oil Futures Contract', 'text': "CME Group announced enhanced product specifications and two additional delivery points for its WTI Houston crude oil futures contracts, pending regulatory review. Beginning with the March 2020 contract expiry, CME Group will require lower sulfur and metals content for deliverable WTI Houston crude to better reflect the prevailing Permian grade crude oil in the U.S. Gulf Coast market. The new requirements will reflect a lower sulfur content of 0.2%, as well as a reduction of vanadium and nickel parameters to an aggregate 3 parts per million (ppm). In addition, and also beginning with the March 2020 contract, suppliers, refiners and end users of U.S. crude oil will have the flexibility to take delivery of U.S. light sweet crude oil at Moore Road Junction, a key distribution point for the Houston, Texas market. Further, in the second quarter of 2020, CME Group intends to include Free On Board (FOB) delivery at export docks located at Enterprise Houston Ship Channel (EHSC), allowing clients to elect to take direct delivery of waterborne WTI Houston Crude Oil (HCL). These two new delivery locations will complement the three existing facilities – Enterprise Crude Houston (ECHO) terminal, the EHSC terminal and Genoa Junction – which have been in place since launch in November 2018. The WTI Houston Crude Oil futures contract expands CME Group's already robust suite of crude oil futures and options and will complement the global benchmark NYMEX WTI Light Sweet Crude Oil futures. Since launch more than 200,000 WTI Houston Crude futures contracts have traded, and the product has reached multiple open interest records during 2019. WTI Houston Crude Oil futures are listed with and subject to the rules of NYMEX."}{'symbol': 'CMCSA', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Comcast Corporation Announces Resignation of David L. Cohen, Senior Executive Vice President', 'text': 'On December 5, 2019, David L. Cohen, Senior Executive Vice President of Comcast Corporation announced that he will step down from his operational responsibilities effective January 1, 2020, and then transition from Senior Executive Vice President to Senior Counselor to Comcast’s Chief Executive Officer beginning December 31, 2020.'}{'symbol': 'STZ', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Kings & Convicts Brewing Co. completed the acquisition of Ballast Point Brewing & Spirits, Inc from Constellation Brands, Inc. (NYSE:STZ).', 'text': 'Kings & Convicts Brewing Co. signed an agreement to acquire Ballast Point Brewing & Spirits, Inc from Constellation Brands, Inc. (NYSE:STZ) on December 3, 2019. As part of this agreement, Kings & Convicts will retain all positions within Ballast Point’s existing workforce, with plans to hire additional resources to support the future growth of the business. This transaction is expected to close by the end of Constellation’s fiscal 2020.\nKings & Convicts Brewing Co. completed the acquisition of Ballast Point Brewing & Spirits, Inc from Constellation Brands, Inc. (NYSE:STZ) on December 5, 2019.\n'}{'symbol': 'COO', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'The Cooper Companies, Inc. Provides Earnings Guidance for the First Quarter and Full Year of 2020', 'text': 'The Cooper Companies, Inc. provided earnings guidance for the first quarter and full year of 2020. For the year 2020, the company fiscal 2020 total revenue $2,767 - $2,817 million (5% to 7% constant currency); CVI revenue $2,070 - $2,100 million (5.5% to 7% constant currency); CSI revenue $697 - $717 million (3% to 6% constant currency). Fiscal first quarter 2020, the company expects total revenue $638 - $653 million (2% to 5% constant currency); CVI revenue $480 - $490 million (3% to 5% constant currency); CSI revenue $158 - $163 million (flat to 4% constant currency).'}{'symbol': 'COST', 'date': '2019-12-05 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Costco Reports Net Sales Of $13.62 Billion For November, Up 6.7%', 'text': 'COSTCO WHOLESALE CORPORATION REPORTS NOVEMBER AND FIRST QUARTER FISCAL YEAR 2020 SALES RESULTS.COSTCO WHOLESALE CORP - E-COMMERCE SALES IN NOVEMBER WERE NEGATIVELY IMPACTED BY AN ESTIMATED 20 PERCENTAGE POINTS.COSTCO WHOLESALE CORP - NET SALES OF $13.62 BILLION FOR NOVEMBER, AN INCREASE OF 6.7 PERCENT FROM $12.77 BILLION LAST YEAR.COSTCO WHOLESALE- TOTAL AND COMPARABLE SALES WERE NEGATIVELY IMPACTED BY APPROXIMATELY ONE AND ONE-HALF PERCENT IN NOV..COSTCO WHOLESALE- FOR 12-WEEK FIRST QUARTER ENDED NOV 24, CO REPORTED NET SALES OF $36.24 BILLION, AN INCREASE OF 5.6 PERCENT.COSTCO WHOLESALE- TOTAL CO COMPARABLE SALES GROWTH FOR TWELVE-WEEK Q1 ENDED NOV 24 OF 4.3%.COSTCO WHOLESALE- U.S. COMPARABLE SALES GROWTH FOR TWELVE-WEEK Q1 ENDED NOV 24 OF 4.7%.COSTCO WHOLESALE CORP - E-COMMERCE COMPARABLE SALES GROWTH FOR 12-WEEK Q1 ENDED NOV 24 OF 5.5%.'}{'symbol': 'DE', 'date': '2019-12-05 17:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Deere & Co Sets Regular Quarterly Dividend Of $0.76 Per Share', 'text': 'SETS REGULAR QUARTERLY DIVIDEND OF $0.76 PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'DG', 'date': '2019-12-05 14:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Dollar General Plans To Expand Non-consumable Offering To Additional 2,600 Stores Next Year - Conf call', 'text': "EXEC - PLAN TO EXPAND NONCONSUMABLE  OFFERING TO ADDITIONAL 2,600 STORES NEXT YEAR, BRINGING TOTAL NCI STORES TO ABOUT 5000 BY 2020  END  - CONF CALL.EXEC - WE HAVE SOME SALES-RELATED HEADWINDS ASSOCIATED WITH THE SHORTENED HOLIDAY SELLING SEASON.DOLLAR GENERAL EXEC - HAVE SOME SALES-RELATED HEADWINDS ASSOCIATED WITH THE LAPPING OF AN ESTIMATED 70 BASIS POINT SALES COMP BENEFIT FROM THE PULL FORWARD OF SNAP PAYMENTS INTO LAST YEAR'S Q4.EXEC -  WE WERE SELF-DISTRIBUTING FROZEN GOODS TO ABOUT 4,900 STORES FROM 4 DG FRESH FACILITIES AT THE END OF Q3.EXEC - EXPECT TO CAPTURE BENEFITS FROM DG FRESH INITIATIVE IN MORE THAN 5,500 STORES BY THE END OF THIS YEAR.EXEC - WE REMAIN ON TRACK TO PILOT DG PICKUP, WHICH IS OUR BUY ONLINE, PICK UP IN STORE OFFERING DURING THE FOURTH QUARTER.EXEC ON FEDEX PARTNERSHIP -  WE EXPECT TO ROLL OUT FEDEX PACKAGE PICKUP & DROP OFF SERVICE IN OVER 8,000 STORES BY 2020 END.EXEC ON SNAP PROGRAM RULE CHANGES - BASED ON WHAT WE KNOW ABOUT THIS PROPOSAL, WE DON'T SEE THIS AS A MATERIAL IMPACT NEXT YEAR.EXEC - WE'RE OVERCOMING TARIFFS. THE TEAM HAS DONE A PHENOMENAL JOB MITIGATING THAT, SUCH THAT IT'S NOT A MATERIAL IMPACT."}{'symbol': 'DG', 'date': '2019-12-05 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Dollar General Q3 Earnings Per Share $1.42', 'text': 'REPORTS STRONG THIRD QUARTER 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.42.Q3 SAME STORE SALES ROSE 4.6 PERCENT.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.38 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $6.55 TO $6.65.SEES FY 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $6.46 TO $6.56.Q3 SALES $7.0 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $6.92 BILLION.RAISES FINANCIAL GUIDANCE FOR FISCAL YEAR 2019.AS OF NOV 1, 2019, TOTAL MERCHANDISE INVENTORIES, AT COST, WERE $4.5 BILLION COMPARED TO $4.0 BILLION AS OF NOV 2, 2018.BOARD INCREASES SHARE REPURCHASE PROGRAM AUTHORIZATION BY $1.0 BILLION.PLANS 1,000 NEW STORE OPENINGS, 1,500 MATURE STORE REMODELS, AND 80 STORE RELOCATIONS IN FISCAL 2020.SEES 2019 NET SALES GROWTH IN THE LOW 8% RANGE, COMPARED TO ITS PREVIOUS EXPECTATION OF APPROXIMATELY 8%.SEES 2019 SAME-STORE SALES GROWTH IN THE MID-TO-HIGH 3% RANGE, COMPARED TO ITS PREVIOUS EXPECTATION IN THE LOW-TO-MID 3% RANGE.DOLLAR GENERAL - FISCAL YEAR 2019 GUIDANCE INCLUDES ANTICIPATED IMPACT OF PREVIOUSLY IMPLEMENTED TARIFF RATES ON CERTAIN PRODUCTS IMPORTED FROM CHINA.CONTINUES TO EXPECT CAPITAL EXPENDITURES IN THE RANGE OF $775 MILLION TO $825 MILLION IN 2019.REITERATING ITS PLANS TO EXECUTE APPROXIMATELY 2,075 REAL ESTATE PROJECTS IN FISCAL YEAR 2019.DOLLAR GENERAL - FISCAL YEAR 2019 FINANCIAL GUIDANCE INCLUDES ANTICIPATED IMPACT OF ADDITIONAL TARIFFS EXPECTED TO BECOME EFFECTIVE ON DEC 15, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'DG', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Dollar General Corporation Declares Cash Dividend, Payable on or Before January 21, 2020', 'text': 'Dollar General Corporation announced Company’s Board of Directors declared a quarterly cash dividend of $0.32 per share on the Company’s common stock, payable on or before January 21, 2020 to shareholders of record on January 7, 2020.'}{'symbol': 'EMN', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Eastman Chemical Company Declares a Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on January 3, 2020', 'text': "The Board of Directors of Eastman Chemical Company has declared a quarterly cash dividend of $0.66 per share on the company's common stock, a 6.5% increase from $0.62 per share. The dividend is payable on Jan. 3, 2020, to stockholders of record as of Dec. 16, 2019."}{'symbol': 'ECL', 'date': '2019-12-05 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ecolab Increases Cash Dividend 2%', 'text': "ECOLAB INCREASES CASH DIVIDEND 2%.ECOLAB - INCREASE IN COMPANY'S QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND TO $0.47 PER COMMON SHARE, TO BE PAID JANUARY 15, 2020."}{'symbol': 'EW', 'date': '2019-12-05 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Edwards Lifesciences Projects 2020 Global Sales Of $4.5-5.0 Bln Underlying Growth 10-12%', 'text': 'EDWARDS LIFESCIENCES CORP - PROJECTED 2020 GLOBAL SALES OF $4.5-5.0 BILLION; UNDERLYING GROWTH 10-12%.EDWARDS LIFESCIENCES CORP - ESTIMATED 2020 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $6.05-6.30.EDWARDS LIFESCIENCES CORP - FOCUSED LONG-TERM GROWTH INVESTMENTS WITH 2020 RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT PLANNED AT 17-18% OF SALES.EDWARDS LIFESCIENCES CORP - EXPECTS TO LAUNCH KONECT RESILIA SYSTEM IN 2020.EDWARDS LIFESCIENCES CORP - EXPECTS TO LAUNCH SUTRAFIX AUTOMATED FASTENING SYSTEM IN LATE 2020.EDWARDS LIFESCIENCES CORP - REAFFIRMING OCTOBER 2019 FINANCIAL GUIDANCE.'}{'symbol': 'EW', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Edwards Lifesciences Corporation Provides Earnings Guidance for the Year 2020', 'text': 'Edwards Lifesciences Corporation provided earnings guidance for the year 2020. For the year, the company expects sales of $4.5 billion to $5.0 billion.'}{'symbol': 'ENPH', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Enphase Energized AC Modules Reach Over 700 Solar Installers in the United States', 'text': 'Enphase Energy, Inc. announced that more than 700 solar installation companies in the U.S. have leveraged Enphase Energized AC Modules (ACMs). Enphase Energized AC Modules, first released in October 2017, are factory-assembled, tested, and sold by Enphase ACM partners, including SunPower, Panasonic, and Solaria. Enphase Energized AC Modules are built by strategic module partners who integrate Enphase microinverters with PV modules on the manufacturing line. ACMs are tested for performance, reliability and quality right on the manufacturing line and allow solar installers to offer premium solutions to homeowners. Enphase Energized AC Modules also help reduce the design complexities associated with high-power modules and provide an ideal combination of high-efficiency modules paired with the most optimal microinverter. When compared to solar installations using combinations of discrete Enphase microinverters and solar modules, ACMs result in a 10-20% reduction in logistics and supply chain overhead, and a 20-40% reduction in system installation time, especially for high-power systems. Enphase Energized AC Modules based on Enphase IQ microinverters meet or exceed regulatory requirements set by the National Electrical Code (NEC) and individual states and are certified compliant with NEC 2014 and 2017 rapid shutdown requirements. Unlike string inverters, Enphase IQ microinverters have rapid shutdown built in, with no additional equipment necessary. Enphase IQ microinverters also comply with requirements for distributed solar on utility networks included in California Rule 21 and Hawaiian Electric Company Rule 14H, such as power factor, voltage, and frequency ride-through requirements.'}{'symbol': 'EXC', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Exelon Corporation Announces Stephen Steinour, Director of Company Not Standing for Election', 'text': 'On December 3, 2019, Exelon Corporation announced that Mr. Stephen Steinour, a director of company, informed the board of directors that he will not stand for election as a director of Exelon at the 2020 annual meeting of shareholders.'}{'symbol': 'FDX', 'date': '2019-12-05 14:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Dollar General Plans To Expand Non-consumable Offering To Additional 2,600 Stores Next Year - Conf call', 'text': "EXEC - PLAN TO EXPAND NONCONSUMABLE  OFFERING TO ADDITIONAL 2,600 STORES NEXT YEAR, BRINGING TOTAL NCI STORES TO ABOUT 5000 BY 2020  END  - CONF CALL.EXEC - WE HAVE SOME SALES-RELATED HEADWINDS ASSOCIATED WITH THE SHORTENED HOLIDAY SELLING SEASON.DOLLAR GENERAL EXEC - HAVE SOME SALES-RELATED HEADWINDS ASSOCIATED WITH THE LAPPING OF AN ESTIMATED 70 BASIS POINT SALES COMP BENEFIT FROM THE PULL FORWARD OF SNAP PAYMENTS INTO LAST YEAR'S Q4.EXEC -  WE WERE SELF-DISTRIBUTING FROZEN GOODS TO ABOUT 4,900 STORES FROM 4 DG FRESH FACILITIES AT THE END OF Q3.EXEC - EXPECT TO CAPTURE BENEFITS FROM DG FRESH INITIATIVE IN MORE THAN 5,500 STORES BY THE END OF THIS YEAR.EXEC - WE REMAIN ON TRACK TO PILOT DG PICKUP, WHICH IS OUR BUY ONLINE, PICK UP IN STORE OFFERING DURING THE FOURTH QUARTER.EXEC ON FEDEX PARTNERSHIP -  WE EXPECT TO ROLL OUT FEDEX PACKAGE PICKUP & DROP OFF SERVICE IN OVER 8,000 STORES BY 2020 END.EXEC ON SNAP PROGRAM RULE CHANGES - BASED ON WHAT WE KNOW ABOUT THIS PROPOSAL, WE DON'T SEE THIS AS A MATERIAL IMPACT NEXT YEAR.EXEC - WE'RE OVERCOMING TARIFFS. THE TEAM HAS DONE A PHENOMENAL JOB MITIGATING THAT, SUCH THAT IT'S NOT A MATERIAL IMPACT."}{'symbol': 'FISV', 'date': '2019-12-05 13:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Motive Partners Acquires Majority Interest In Investment Services Business Of Fiserv', 'text': 'MOTIVE PARTNERS ACQUIRES MAJORITY INTEREST IN INVESTMENT SERVICES BUSINESS OF FISERV.MOTIVE PARTNERS - ENTERED INTO AGREEMENT UNDER WHICH MOTIVE PARTNERS-LED INVESTORS WILL ACQUIRE UP TO 60% OF INVESTMENT SERVICES BUSINESS OF FISERV.MOTIVE PARTNERS- RETAINING A 40% EQUITY INTEREST IN BUSINESS, FISERV WILL RECEIVE APPROXIMATELY $510 MILLION IN NET AFTER-TAX PROCEEDS.FISERV INC - NEWLY FORMED JOINT VENTURE WILL CONTINUE TO BE LED BY CHERYL NASH, PRESIDENT OF INVESTMENT SERVICES AT FISERV.MOTIVE PARTNERS- TRANSACTION EXPECTED TO BE SLIGHTLY DILUTIVE TO ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE OF FISERV IN 2020..'}{'symbol': 'FISV', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Motive Partners and Fiserv, Inc. Announce Executive Changes', 'text': 'Motive Partners and Fiserv, Inc. have entered into a definitive agreement under which Motive Partners-led investors will acquire up to 60% of the Investment Services business of Fiserv. Retaining a 40% equity interest in the business, Fiserv will receive approximately $510 million in net after-tax proceeds. The newly formed joint venture will continue to be led by Cheryl Nash, President of Investment Services at Fiserv. Upon the closing of the transaction, Rob Heyvaert, Founder and Managing Partner of Motive Partners, will serve as Executive Chairman of the joint venture. William P.  Foley II, Executive Chairman of Cannae Holdings, Dun & Bradstreet and Black Knight and Alvi Abuaf, lead Industry Partner for Motive Partners, will also join the Board.'}{'symbol': 'F', 'date': '2019-12-05 03:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'KPMG LLP Says To Provide Global Tax Compliance Services To Ford Motor Company', 'text': "KPMG LLP - CO TO PROVIDE GLOBAL TAX COMPLIANCE SERVICES TO FORD MOTOR COMPANY.KPMG - TO PROVIDE DIRECT AND INDIRECT TAX COMPLIANCE SERVICES FOR SELECT SET OF COMPANY'S OPERATIONS ACROSS EUROPE, ASIA AND LATIN AMERICA."}{'symbol': 'GD', 'date': '2019-12-05 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'General Dynamics Sets Regular Quarterly Dividend Of $1.02 Per Share', 'text': 'SETS REGULAR QUARTERLY DIVIDEND OF $1.02PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'GIS', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'General Mills, Inc. Elects Mark Pallot as Vice President, Chief Accounting Officer and Principal Accounting Officer, Effective February 1, 2020', 'text': "On December 2, 2019, the board of directors of General Mills, Inc. elected Mark Pallot as Vice President, Chief Accounting Officer effective February 1, 2020. In this role, Mr. Pallot will serve as the Company's principal accounting officer. Mr. Pallot, age 46, has served as the Company's Vice President, Assistant Controller since August 2017. Prior to that, Mr. Pallot served as the Company's Director of Financial Reporting from 2007 to July 2017."}{'symbol': 'GM', 'date': '2019-12-05 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'General Motors And LG Chem Form JV To Make Battery Cells In Ohio', 'text': "GENERAL MOTORS SAYS CO AND LG CHEM FORM JOINT VENTURE TO MAKE BATTERY CELLS IN OHIO.GENERAL MOTORS SAYS CO, LG CHEM TO INVEST $2.3 BILLION IN NEW PLANT NEAR LORDSTOWN.GENERAL MOTORS SAYS JV WILL JOINTLY DEVELOP ADVANCED BATTERY TECHNOLOGIES.GENERAL MOTORS SAYS FACILITY WILL EMPLOY UP TO 1,100 WORKERS, HAVING ANNUAL CAPACITY OF MORE THAN 30 GIGAWATT-HOURS, WITH FLEXIBILITY FOR EXPANSION.GENERAL MOTORS SAYS PLANT WILL BE ONE OF WORLD'S LARGEST BATTERY FACILITIES."}{'symbol': 'GS', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'GTT Communications, Inc. Chooses Credit Suisse and Goldman Sachs as Financial Advisors for Infrastructure Division Sale', 'text': "GTT Communications, Inc. has selected Credit Suisse and Goldman Sachs to act as financial advisors to the company in connection with the potential sale of the Infrastructure Division, which includes the company's highly differentiated terrestrial pan-European fiber network, subsea transatlantic fiber and data center infrastructure that were part of the Interoute and Hibernia acquisitions."}{'symbol': 'HAS', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Hasbro, Inc. Declares Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on February 18, 2020', 'text': 'Hasbro, Inc. announced that its board of directors has declared a quarterly cash dividend of $0.68 per common share. The dividend will be payable on February 18, 2020 to shareholders of record at the close of business on February 1, 2020.'}{'symbol': 'HES', 'date': '2019-12-05 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Hess Declares Regular Quarterly Dividend Of 25 Cents Per Share', 'text': 'HESS CORP - DECLARED A REGULAR QUARTERLY DIVIDEND OF 25 CENTS PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'HOLX', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Hologic, Inc. Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fiscal Year 2020', 'text': 'Hologic, Inc. provided earnings guidance for the fiscal year 2020. For this period, the company expects EPS guidance range to be $2.60 to $2.65.'}{'symbol': 'IBM', 'date': '2019-12-05 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'IBM Says New Agreement With Aegean To Use IBM Public Cloud', 'text': 'IBM - NEW AGREEMENT WITH AEGEAN TO USE IBM PUBLIC CLOUD.'}{'symbol': 'IBM', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'AEGEAN Airlines Selects IBM to Deliver Innovative Customer Experiences', 'text': "IBM announced a new agreement with AEGEAN to use IBM public cloud to transform its internal business processes and further enhance its customer experience. This agreement follows a multi-year agreement for the implementation of core applications and the delivery of IBM Cloud Hosting Services to help accelerate the airline's digital transformation strategy. Operating in a highly competitive industry, AEGEAN, and its subsidiary Olympic Air, has gone to great lengths to improve efficiencies and customer experience by investing in disruptive technologies, including cloud and AI. By leveraging IBM public cloud, AEGEAN aims to increase process efficiency, support company growth with reduced operational costs and drive innovation through the use of higher value technology. AEGEAN will work with IBM Services to utilize innovative technology solutions, including advanced business analytics capabilities that enable data driven decision making. With IBM public cloud, AEGEAN is able to infuse AI into its decisions support systems and use IBM Watson Studio and IBM Watson Machine Learning solutions to gain better business insights, identifying operational efficiencies and supporting their network and pricing strategy. By taking advantage of IBM's services capabilities, advanced analytics and industry expertise, AEGEAN is seeking to improve business operations through process standardization in a reliable, scalable and agile environment."}{'symbol': 'IPG', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'The Interpublic Group of Companies Continues to Expand with Empire State Realty Trust', 'text': "Empire State Realty Trust, Inc. announced that The Interpublic Group of Companies, Inc. signed a 15,086 square foot lease on the 30th floor of 1400 Broadway. This expansion will increase the footprint of The Interpublic Group of Companies within ESRT's portfolio to 127,781 sq. ft. located at 1400 Broadway and 111 W. 33rd St."}{'symbol': 'JNJ', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Johnson & Johnson Announces Board Appointments', 'text': 'Johnson & Johnson announced that Hubert Joly, Executive Chairman of Best Buy Co., Inc, and Mark A. Weinberger, Former EY Global Chairman and CEO, have been appointed to its Board of Directors. Hubert Joly brings deep strategic, operational and financial expertise that spans more than three decades. Mr. Joly currently serves as Executive Chairman of Best Buy Co., Inc, having previously served as Chief Executive Officer and then as Chairman and CEO from 2012 until 2019. Mark Weinberger brings more than three decades of global leadership expertise across both the public and private sectors. In his former role as Global Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of EY, Mr. Weinberger led one of the largest global professional services organization in the world that provides assurance, tax, transaction and advisory services.'}{'symbol': 'JPM', 'date': '2019-12-05 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Envestnet Inc And JP Morgan Chase Sign A Data Sharing Agreement', 'text': 'ENVESTNET INC - CO AND JPMORGAN CHASE HAVE SIGNED A DATA SHARING AGREEMENT.ENVESTNET - UNDER TERMS, JP MORGAN CHASE CUSTOMERS SEND FINANCIAL INFORMATION TO MORE THAN 1,200 THIRD-PARTY APPLICATIONS ON ENVESTNET PLATFORM.'}{'symbol': 'KEYS', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Keysight Technologies, Inc and Marvin Test Solutions Collaborates to Speed Manufacturing of mmWave Semiconductors', 'text': 'Keysight Technologies, Inc. announced that its collaboration with Marvin Test Solutions, Inc, a supplier of functional test solutions – has resulted in the development of a fast and accurate 5G semiconductor manufacturing test platform. The two parties focused on advancing beamformer integrated circuit (IC) test technology to help manufacturers of semiconductors accelerate the production of high performance 5G integrated ICs. Marvin – a trusted provider of globally-deployed test solutions for military, aerospace, and manufacturing organizations – integrated Keysight’s PXIe-based Vector Network Analyzer (VNA) to achieve accurate and fast measurements in its TS-960e-5G mmWave Test System. Keysight’s recently introduced M980xA Series network analyzers offer the scalability required to test multi-port components, front end modules (FEMs) and base stations that rely on beamforming technology. Mobile operators are deploying beamforming technology to extend cellular coverage and deliver higher data rates, leading to improved mmWave 5G network reliability and efficiency. To ensure reliable and efficient 5G mmWave communications, the performance of critical elements that form part of the beamformer IC need to be rigorously tested under linear and nonlinear conditions across the entire workflow from design, validation to manufacturing.'}{'symbol': 'KMI', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Kinder Morgan, Inc. Provides Dividend Guidance for the First Quarter and Full Year of 2020', 'text': 'Kinder Morgan, Inc. provided dividend guidance for the first quarter and full year of 2020. The company expects to increase the declared dividend per common share in 2020 to $1.25 per share (annualized), beginning with $0.3125 per share for the first quarter 2020 dividend (which will be paid in the second quarter 2020).'}{'symbol': 'KR', 'date': '2019-12-05 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Kroger Reports Q3 Adjusted EPS Of $0.47', 'text': "KROGER REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 SALES $28 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $28.2 BILLION.QTRLY EPS OF $0.32; ADJUSTED EPS OF $0.47 WHICH INCLUDES A $0.03 OUT OF PERIOD CHARGE.QTRLY IDENTICAL SALES WITHOUT FUEL GREW 2.5% AND DIGITAL SALES GREW 21%.CONFIRMS IDENTICAL SALES, ADJUSTED FIFO OPERATING PROFIT AND ADJUSTED EPS GUIDANCE FOR 2019 AND 2020.SEES 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.17 - $2.27.QTRLY EPS AFFECTED BY SEVERAL ADJUSTMENT ITEMS, PRIMARILY BY A NON-CASH IMPAIRMENT CHARGE RELATED TO AN INVESTMENT IN LUCKY'S MARKET.ALTERNATIVE PROFIT STREAMS ON TRACK TO CONTRIBUTE AN INCREMENTAL $100 MILLION IN OPERATING PROFIT IN 2019 VERSUS. 2018.SEES 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.15 - $2.25.SEES 2020 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.30 - $2.40.SEES 2020 CAP EX $3.2-$3.4 BILLION.SEES 2019 CAP EX $3.0 BILLION - $3.2 BILLION.SEES 2020 ADJUSTED FCF $1.6-$1.8 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.49 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES 2020 SHARE REPURCHASE OF $500 MILLION -$1,000 MILLION.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.20 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.23 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA."}{'symbol': 'KR', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'the Kroger Co. Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended November 9, 2019', 'text': 'The Kroger Co. Announced earnings results for the third quarter ended November 9, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced sales was USD 27,974 million compared to USD 27,831 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 254 million compared to USD 647 million a year ago. Net income was USD 263 million compared to USD 317 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 0.32 compared to USD 0.39 a year ago. For the nine months, sales was USD 93,393 million compared to USD 93,566 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 1,714 million compared to USD 2,225 million a year ago. Net income was USD 1,332 million compared to USD 2,851 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 1.65 compared to USD 3.46 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 1.64 compared to USD 3.43 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'LLY', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Eli Lilly Says Combining Lilly Research Laboratories Oncology Organization And Loxo Oncology', 'text': 'Dec 5  - Eli Lilly and Co <LLY.N>::LILLY ANNOUNCES NEW LEADERSHIP AND STRATEGY IN ONCOLOGY RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT.ELI LILLY AND CO - NEW ORGANIZATION, NAMED LOXO ONCOLOGY AT LILLY, WILL BE LED JOINTLY BY JOSH BILENKER, , JACOB VAN NAARDEN, AND NISHA NANDA.ELI LILLY AND CO - COMBINING LILLY RESEARCH LABORATORIES ONCOLOGY ORGANIZATION AND LOXO ONCOLOGY.'}{'symbol': 'MAR', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "ASMALLWORLD AG Announces North Island Resort Joins Marriott's the Luxury Collection", 'text': "ASMALLWORLD AG announced that North Island resort joined Marriott International's The Luxury Collection brand portfolio. The Seychelles luxury resort, managed by ASMALLWORLD, can now be booked through Marriott's distribution channels, which will broaden the awareness of the resort and its unique, sustainable management philosophy. The resort offers a pioneering conservation program as well as the highest standards of hospitality, earning it status as a sustainable travel destination. The mission to demonstrate that luxury and conscience can co-exist, lies at the heart of North Island's philosophy. Under the new partnership with Marriott, North Island now joins The Luxury Collection, which is comprised of hotels offering unique, authentic experiences that evoke lasting, treasured memories. The partnership will further increase the awareness of the iconic resort and its unique character and philosophy. North Island can now be booked through Marriott's established and far-reaching distribution channels and the resort will also participate in Marriott's Bonvoy loyalty program. The operational responsibility of the resort will remain with ASMALLWORLD."}{'symbol': 'MAR', 'date': '2019-12-05 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Marriott Says Projecting To Open More Than 30 Luxury Properties In 2020', 'text': 'MARRIOTT - PROJECTING TO OPEN MORE THAN 30 LUXURY PROPERTIES IN 2020.'}{'symbol': 'MA', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Mastercard Partners with Seven Fintechs to Promote Digital Payments', 'text': "Mastercard has partnered with seven fintech start-ups from around the world to promote the adoption of digital payments. The selected partners will join Mastercard's Accelerate programme. They will be provided with operational support and business opportunities within the Mastercard ecosystem. They will join Mastercard's start-up engagement platform known as Start Path, where later-stage start-ups are called to take part in a six-month virtual programme. The participants are also given opportunities to expand and get investments. Mastercard has chosen the seven start-ups after searching 210 countries across the world. The selected start-ups are BharatPe, Cyberwrite, Hydrogen, Eureka AI, Kasha, mmuze, and Ziosk. India-based B2B payments start-up BharatPe operates as a digital bank, Cyberwrite offers its SaaS platform to protect against cyber risk, while Eureka AI helps firms to tap the power of AI. Hydrogen allows users to build modern financial applications using a single platform, Kasha manages an e-commerce platform in Africa, mmuze operates as a voice-shopping platform, and Ziosk offers pay-on-demand solution for casual dining restaurants. Mastercard founded its Start Path accelerator programme in 2014. Using this programme, the American payment technology firm assesses thousands of start-ups and chooses nearly 40 promising firms on an annual basis. Through its Start Path programme, Mastercard has so far selected over 200 start-ups that have raised $1.5 billion in funding."}{'symbol': 'MRK', 'date': '2019-12-05 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Lynparza (Olaparib) Approved In China As A First-Line Maintenance Therapy In BRCA-Mutated (BRCAm) Advanced Ovarian Cancer', 'text': 'LYNPARZA® (OLAPARIB) APPROVED IN CHINA AS A FIRST-LINE MAINTENANCE THERAPY IN BRCA-MUTATED (BRCAM) ADVANCED OVARIAN CANCER.MERCK & CO INC - LYNPARZA APPROVAL IN CHINA IS BASED ON RESULTS FROM PIVOTAL PHASE 3 SOLO-1 TRIAL.'}{'symbol': 'MET', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'MetLife, Inc. (NYSE:MET) entered into a definitive agreement to acquire PetFirst Healthcare LLC.', 'text': 'MetLife, Inc. (NYSE:MET) entered into a definitive agreement to acquire PetFirst Healthcare LLC on December 5, 2019. PetFirst has about 60 employees in its Jeffersonville offices and all are expected to continue in their current or similar positions. The transaction is subject to customary closing conditions and approvals and is expected to close in the first quarter of 2020. Guggenheim Securities, LLC acted as the financial advisor and Mayer Brown LLP acted as the legal advisor to MetLife, Inc.\n'}{'symbol': 'MSFT', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "KPMG and Microsoft Sign Five-Year Agreement to Enable KPMG Member Firms and Mutual Clients to Benefit from Microsoft Technology, Innovation and Advancements in Microsoft's Cloud Platforms", 'text': "KPMG announced investments in technology, people and innovation, and expects to spend USD 5 billion over the next five years to enhance its leadership position in the digital transformation of professional services. KPMG enters five-year agreement with Microsoft to invest in cloud-based technologies. As part of this investment, KPMG and Microsoft have signed a five-year agreement that enables KPMG member firms and mutual clients to benefit from Microsoft technology, innovation and advancements in Microsoft's cloud platforms. KPMG is utilizing Microsoft technology 'including Microsoft Azure and Microsoft 365' to create a consistent, global cloud-based platform and extend its range of digital offerings. KPMG fully deploying cloud-based audit across the globe."}{'symbol': 'MSFT', 'date': '2019-12-05 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Microsoft Sets Quarterly Dividend Of $0.51 Per Share', 'text': 'SETS QUARTERLY DIVIDEND OF $0.51PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'MDLZ', 'date': '2019-12-05 15:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Mondelēz International Declares Regular Quarterly Dividend Of $0.285 Per Share', 'text': 'MONDELĒZ INTERNATIONAL DECLARES REGULAR QUARTERLY DIVIDEND OF $0.285 PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'MDLZ', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Mondelez International, Inc. Declares Regular Quarterly Dividend, Payable on January 14, 2020', 'text': 'The Board of Directors of Mondelez International, Inc. declared a regular quarterly dividend of $0.285 per share of Class A common stock. This dividend is payable on January 14, 2020, to shareholders of record as of December 31, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'NTRS', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Northern Trust Announces Appointment of Executives', 'text': 'Northern Trust announced the appointment of two senior business development executives to its Global Foreign Exchange Solutions practice in North America. David Byne and William Hartnett will be responsible for driving growth across the full range of FX solutions at Northern Trust, including algorithmic trading, CompleteFX™ (outsourced end-to-end FX dealing service), and Currency Management. Hartnett, based in Chicago, has more than a decade of foreign exchange experience, serving in several trading and sales roles before transitioning to business development. Prior to Northern Trust, Hartnett served as an FX options trader on the Chicago Board of Trade and at Fifth Third Bank. Byne brings almost 15 years of foreign exchange experience to Northern Trust. Before joining Northern Trust, Byne held a number of FX-related positions at Credit Suisse and Citi, among others.'}{'symbol': 'PM', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Philip Morris International Inc. Declares Regular Quarterly Dividend, Payable on January 10, 2020', 'text': 'The Board of Directors of Philip Morris International Inc. declared a regular quarterly dividend of $1.17 per common share, payable on January 10, 2020, to shareholders of record as of December 19, 2019. The ex-dividend date is December 18, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'PLD', 'date': '2019-12-05 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Prologis Announces Expansion Of Development Venture In China And Increases Development Capacity To More Than $3.5 Billion', 'text': 'PROLOGIS INC -  ANNOUNCED EXPANSION OF ITS DEVELOPMENT VENTURE IN CHINA AND INCREASED ITS DEVELOPMENT CAPACITY TO MORE THAN US$3.5 BILLION.PROLOGIS INC - ANNOUNCED FORMATION OF ITS NEW US$1.7 BILLION OPEN-ENDED PROLOGIS CHINA CORE LOGISTICS FUND LP.PROLOGIS - HIP CHINA LOGISTICS INVESTMENTS LIMITED, CO COMMITTED ADDITIONAL US$882 MILLION OF EQUITY FOR EXPANSION OF PROLOGIS CHINA LOGISTICS VENTURE 3.PROLOGIS INC - PROLOGIS AND HIP WILL RETAIN THEIR RESPECTIVE OWNERSHIP PERCENTAGES IN PROLOGIS CHINA LOGISTICS VENTURE 3.PROLOGIS INC - ALSO ANNOUNCED FORMATION OF PCCLF, A PERPETUAL LIFE FUND.PROLOGIS INC - WILL MAINTAIN ITS OWNERSHIP PERCENTAGE AND HIP WILL CONTINUE TO BE A MAJOR INVESTOR IN PCCLF.'}{'symbol': 'PHM', 'date': '2019-12-05 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'PulteGroup Increases Quarterly Cash Dividend By 9% To $0.12 Per Share', 'text': 'PULTEGROUP INCREASES QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND BY 9% TO $0.12 PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'PHM', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'PulteGroup, Inc. Increases Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on January 3, 2020', 'text': 'PulteGroup, Inc. announced that its Board of Directors has voted to approve a 9% increase in the company’s quarterly cash dividend to $0.12 per common share. The increase is effective with the company’s next dividend which is payable January 3, 2020, to shareholders of record at the close of business on December 18, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'QCOM', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Qualcomm Officially Announces Its Next-Generation Processor for Phones', 'text': "Qualcomm officially announced its next-generation processor for phones. Dubbed the Snapdragon 865 the processor is still in need of a separate 5G modem to enable 5G instead of an integrated 5G modem built right into the chipset. Traditionally, that means more expensive, power-hungry phones than an integrated solution. However, at the Amazons event held in Las Vegas called AWS re:Invent, there were plenty of other solutions. Verizon CEO Hans Vestberg went on to discuss the company's partnership with the Amazon-owned cloud computing giant. As part of Verizons upcoming focus on 5G edge computing, the company will be the first to use the newly announced AWS Wavelength. The platform is made in a way it enables developers to create super-low-latency apps for 5G devices. For now, the pilot of this project was introduced in Chicago with numerous high-profile partners, including the NFL and Bethesda, the game developer behind Fallout and Elder Scrolls. However, there are still no details about those specific applications (we can only presume that the remote gaming and live streaming could be one of those), but potential future uses include things like smart cars, IoT devices, AR/VR, etc."}{'symbol': 'REGN', 'date': '2019-12-05 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Regeneron Announces Positive Topline Data From Rare Blood Disorder Study', 'text': 'REGENERON ANNOUNCES POSITIVE TOPLINE PHASE 2 DATA WITH ANTI-C5 ANTIBODY POZELIMAB IN PATIENTS WITH A RARE BLOOD DISORDER.REGENERON PHARMACEUTICALS INC - SECOND PART OF PHASE 2 TRIAL INITIATED.REGENERON PHARMAC- POZELIMAB REDUCED ABNORMAL DESTRUCTION OF RED BLOOD CELLS WITH PATIENTS IN INITIAL COHORT ACHIEVING NORMAL LEVELS OF BLOOD BIOMARKER.REGENERON PHARMACEUTICALS INC - IN EARLIER PHASE 1 TRIAL, ONLY SERIOUS AE WAS SALPINGITIS IN A SINGLE PARTICIPANT.'}{'symbol': 'REGN', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, Inc Announces Positive Topline Phase 2 Data with Anti-C5 Antibody Pozelimab in Patients with a Rare Blood Disorder', 'text': 'Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, Inc. announced topline data from the pozelimab (REGN3918) Phase 2 clinical program in paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria (PNH), validating the weekly 800 mg subcutaneous (SC) dosing regimen, following an initial intravenous (IV) loading dose. Pozelimab reduced the abnormal destruction of red blood cells, otherwise known as "hemolysis," with patients in the initial cohort achieving normal levels of a blood biomarker of elevated hemolysis called lactate dehydrogenase (LDH). PNH is an ultra-rare, chronic, life-threatening disease where genetic mutations cause hemolysis, resulting in a range of symptoms including fatigue, shortness of breath and blood clots. Even with existing therapies, which require regular intravenous infusions administered at infusion centers or during a home visit by a health professional, approximately 50% of newly-treated patients do not achieve normal LDH levels. Pozelimab is a VelocImmune®-derived fully-human monoclonal antibody that blocks the pathway leading to red blood cell hemolysis, which was designed to reduce LDH levels and the occurrence of breakthrough hemolysis, using a self-administered subcutaneous regimen. All 6 patients in the initial treatment cohort treated with pozelimab experienced rapid and sustained reductions in LDH up to week 8. By week 2, LDH was reduced to <1.5 times the upper limit of normal (ULN) in all patients, and at the pre-specified week 8 evaluation timepoint, the mean LDH level was 0.74 (x ULN); range: 0.62-0.91 (x ULN). One of these patients had a known C5 variant resistant to existing treatments. In these 6 patients, no adverse events (AEs) were serious or led to discontinuation. At the cut-off date of the analyses, treatment-related AEs were reported in 3 patients (50%), including headache (n=2), injection site reaction (n=1) and nausea (n=1). One patient received a blood transfusion on day 50 due to underlying bone marrow dysfunction. In the earlier Phase 1 trial, the only serious AE was salpingitis in a single participant.'}{'symbol': 'RCL', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Royal Caribbean Cruises Ltd. Declares Quarterly Dividend, Payable on January 6, 2020', 'text': 'The Board of Directors of Royal Caribbean Cruises Ltd. declared a quarterly dividend of $0.78 per common share payable on January 6, 2020, to shareholders of record at the close of business on December 20, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'SYK', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Stryker Corporation Announces Retirement of Louise L. Francesconi from the Board', 'text': 'On November 29, 2019, Ms. Louise L. Francesconi, a member of the Board of Directors of Stryker Corporation informed the company that she plans to retire as a director and will not stand for re-election to the board at the company’s annual shareholders meeting expected to be held on May 5, 2020. Ms. Francesconi will continue to serve as a director until the Annual Meeting. Ms. Francesconi’s decision to not stand for re-election did not involve any disagreement with the Company.'}{'symbol': 'SYK', 'date': '2019-12-05 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Stryker Declares $0.575 Per Share Quarterly Dividend', 'text': 'STRYKER INCREASES DIVIDEND 11%, DECLARING A $0.575 PER SHARE QUARTERLY DIVIDEND.'}{'symbol': 'SNPS', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Synopsys Collaborates with Google Cloud to Broadly Scale Cloud-Based Functional Verification', 'text': 'Synopsys, Inc.\xa0announced a collaboration with Google Cloud to provide a full end-to-end solution to perform functional verification workloads in the cloud. An increasing number of users are seeking solutions that take advantage of the elastic hardware scalability offered in the cloud to address peak/burst simulation capacity requirements, enabling a higher quality verification on a predictable schedule. This collaboration provides a proven and scalable solution to enable Synopsys VCS® simulation workloads on Google Cloud. Moving verification workloads to the cloud brings a unique set of challenges, such as hardware instance selection, file system configuration, and job orchestration. Using proven infrastructure to ensure efficient utilization of resources and native Google Cloud NetApp integration to bridge the on-premises and cloud infrastructures, together with tight integration between VCS and Google Cloud Preemptible VM instances, enables VCS users to quickly take advantage of the elastic resources available in the cloud.'}{'symbol': 'SNPS', 'date': '2019-12-05 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Synopsys Posts Quarterly GAAP Earnings Per Share Of $1.04', 'text': 'SYNOPSYS POSTS FINANCIAL RESULTS FOR FOURTH QUARTER AND FISCAL YEAR 2019.Q4 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $4.56.Q4 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.04.Q4 REVENUE $851.1 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $847.3 MILLION.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.13 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'TEL', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'TE Connectivity Introduces its Thermal Bridge Technology', 'text': "TE Connectivity is introducing its thermal bridge technology that can provide up to two times better thermal resistance over traditional thermal technologies such as gap pads or thermal pads. As systems like servers, switches and routers deliver higher speeds and grow more sophisticated, their power requirements are rising, leading to a need for new solutions that can handle more heat. TE's thermal bridge solution offers superior thermal resistance, better reliability and durability, and allows for easier system serviceability than other comparable products on the market. Optimized for input/output (I/O) applications using cold plates with liquid cooling or heat pipes, ganged heatsinks or direct chassis conduction applications with little to no airflow, TE's thermal bridge solutions feature a near-zero plate gap in the bridge construction for substantially improved thermal transfer and minimal levels of compression. In addition, the new solution delivers long-lasting and consistent thermal performance with an elastic compression design that is resistant to set or relaxation over time. This feature also helps to reduce component replacement during system servicing. The thermal bridge comes pre-assembled on the I/O cage and features an interleaved series of plates that allows heat to pass from the I/O module to the cooling area, while providing the necessary normal force, which is built into the thermal bridge. TE's thermal bridge solutions are currently available for sample in SFP+, QSFP28 and QSFP-DD form factors."}{'symbol': 'TER', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Teradyne Marks the 6,000th J750 Semiconductor Test System Shipment with Ardentec', 'text': 'Teradyne, Inc. announced the 6,000th shipment of the J750 family of semiconductor testers. The J750 family includes wafer sort and final test solutions for Microcontroller Units (MCUs), wireless devices and image sensors. Ardentec, with one of the largest installed bases of J750 testers, received Teradyne’s 6,000th shipment. Teradyne’s J750 family is the world leading MCU device testing solution for automotive and consumer applications and the worldwide leader in image sensor testing. The scalability of the test system makes it ideal for the low cost devices with increasing feature integration and extending to fingerprint sensors, MEMS and MCU’s wireless capability supporting Internet of Things (IoT). The J750 family operates using IG-XLTM software platform for rapid program development that automatically scales to support multisite testing saving significant development time and cost. Teradyne’s J750 family is the industry standard for test quality while semiconductor manufacturers pursue zero-defect goals combined with multisite throughput. With an installed base now over 6,000, the test systems are widely available at more than 50 Outsourced Semiconductor Assembly and Test (OSAT) locations and are supported by a complete set of production interface solutions for wafer sort and final test.'}{'symbol': 'TSCO', 'date': '2019-12-05 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Tractor Supply Company Names Hal Lawton President And Chief Executive Officer', 'text': "TRACTOR SUPPLY COMPANY ANNOUNCES CEO SUCCESSION PLAN; NAMES HAL LAWTON PRESIDENT AND CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER, EFFECTIVE JANUARY 13, 2020.TRACTOR SUPPLY CO - GREG SANDFORT WILL REMAIN AS ADVISOR AND ON BOARD OF DIRECTORS TO SUPPORT TRANSITION.TRACTOR SUPPLY CO - HAL LAWTON, WHO IS CURRENTLY PRESIDENT OF MACY'S, WILL SUCCEED TRACTOR SUPPLY'S CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER GREG SANDFORT.TRACTOR SUPPLY CO - SANDFORT WILL REMAIN WITH CO THROUGH FEB 29, 2020, & THEN SERVE AS ADVISOR UNTIL AUGUST 31, 2020, TO ENSURE A SEAMLESS TRANSITION."}{'symbol': 'ULTA', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ulta Beauty, Inc. Revises Earnings Guidance for the Fiscal Year 2019; to Open Approximately 80 New Stores', 'text': 'Ulta Beauty, Inc. revised earnings guidance for the fiscal year 2019. For the year, the company expected increase of total sales by approximately 10% (previously between 9% and 12%). The company expected to deliver diluted earnings per share in the range of $11.93 to $12.03 (previously $11.86 to $12.06).The company expected to open approximately 80 new stores, execute approximately 20 remodel or relocation projects, and complete approximately 270 store refreshes.'}{'symbol': 'UAL', 'date': '2019-12-05 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'United Airlines Says Scott Kirby, President, To Become Chief Executive Officer', 'text': "UNITED AIRLINES ANNOUNCES LEADERSHIP TRANSITION.UNITED AIRLINES HOLDINGS INC - OSCAR MUNOZ, CEO, TO BECOME EXECUTIVE CHAIRMAN OF BOARD OF DIRECTORS.UNITED AIRLINES HOLDINGS INC - CHANGES TO TAKE EFFECT FOLLOWING ANNUAL MEETING OF SHAREHOLDERS ON MAY 20, 2020.UNITED AIRLINES HOLDINGS INC - SCOTT KIRBY, PRESIDENT, TO BECOME CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER.UNITED AIRLINES HOLDINGS INC - TED PHILIP TO BECOME LEAD INDEPENDENT DIRECTOR OF BOARD OF DIRECTORS.UNITED AIRLINES HOLDINGS INC - UNITED'S CURRENT CHAIRMAN, JANE GARVEY, WILL RETIRE FROM BOARD IN MAY 2020.UNITED AIRLINES HOLDINGS INC - MUNOZ WILL SERVE AS EXECUTIVE CHAIRMAN FOR A ONE-YEAR TERM.UNITED AIRLINES HOLDINGS - GARVEY AGREED TO REMAIN IN HER ROLE FOR A YEAR BEYOND BOARD'S MANDATORY RETIREMENT AGE.UNITED AIRLINES HOLDINGS - TED PHILIP ALSO CURRENTLY SERVES ON BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF HASBRO, INC. AND BRP INC."}{'symbol': 'UAL', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'United Airlines Holdings, Inc. Announces Management Changes', 'text': "United Airlines Holdings, Inc. announced that Oscar Munoz, Chief Executive Officer, will transition to the role of Executive Chairman of the Board of Directors in May 2020. As CEO, Munoz has transformed United's culture and set new standards of operational and financial performance. J. Scott Kirby, President, will succeed Munoz as Chief Executive Officer. Kirby was recruited to United Airlines by Munoz in August 2016, after a three-decade career in the commercial airline business. His appointment reflects a commitment from Munoz and the Board to preserve leadership continuity and demonstrates confidence in the airline's strategy and current trajectory. Munoz will serve as Executive Chairman for a one-year term and will continue to work closely with Kirby, the Board and the United team in shaping United's employee and customer-centric culture. He will also lead the company's Board and continue to engage on behalf of United with a range of external stakeholders. The company also announced that Ted Philip will become Lead Independent Director following the 2020 Annual Meeting of Shareholders. Philip joined the Board in July 2016 and chairs the Nominating/Governance Committee. He also currently serves on the Board of Directors of Hasbro, Inc. and BRP Inc. All of the changes announced will take effect following the company's Annual Meeting of Shareholders, scheduled for May 20, 2020."}{'symbol': 'VZ', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Verizon Communications Inc. Declares Quarterly Dividend, Payable on February 3, 2020', 'text': 'The Board of Directors of Verizon Communications Inc. declared a quarterly dividend of 61.50 cents per outstanding share, unchanged from the previous quarter. The quarterly dividend is payable on February 3, 2020, to Verizon shareowners of record at the close of business on January 10, 2020.'}{'symbol': 'VIAC', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ViacomCBS Inc. has filed a Shelf Registration in the amount of $763.476918 million.', 'text': 'ViacomCBS Inc. has filed a Shelf Registration in the amount of $763.476918 million.\n\nSecurity Name: Class B Common Stock\nSecurities Offered: 18,726,439\nTransaction Features: ESOP Related Offering'}{'symbol': 'VIAC', 'date': '2019-12-05 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ViacomCBS Announces Completion Of The Merger Of CBS And Viacom', 'text': 'VIACOMCBS ANNOUNCES COMPLETION OF THE MERGER OF CBS AND VIACOM.'}{'symbol': 'V', 'date': '2019-12-05 15:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Visa Inc Says CEO Alfred Kelly's FY 2019 Total Compensation Was $24.3 Mln", 'text': "VISA INC SAYS CFO VASANT M. PRABHU'S FY 2019 TOTAL COMPENSATION WAS $11.6 MILLION VERSUS $12.6 MILLION IN FY 2018 - SEC FILING.VISA INC SAYS CEO ALFRED KELLY'S FY 2019 TOTAL COMPENSATION WAS $24.3 MILLION VERSUS $19.5 MILLION IN FY 2018 - SEC FILING.VISA INC SAYS PRESIDENT RYAN MCINERNEY'S FY 2019 TOTAL COMPENSATION WAS $12.1 MILLION VERSUS $13.3 MILLION IN FY 2018.VISA INC SAYS PRESIDENT OF TECHNOLOGY RAJAT TANEJA'S FY 2019 TOTAL COMPENSATION WAS $11.8 MILLION VERSUS $13.2 MILLION IN FY 2018 - SEC FILING.VISA INC SAYS FY 2019 PAY RATIO OF CEO TO MEDIAN EMPLOYEES ANNUAL TOTAL COMPENSATION IS 170:1."}{'symbol': 'WRB', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'W. R. Berkley Corporation(NYSE:WRB) dropped from S&P 400 Financials (Sector)', 'text': 'W. R. Berkley Corporation(NYSE:WRB) dropped from S&P 400 Financials (Sector)'}{'symbol': 'DIS', 'date': '2019-12-05 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'The Walt Disney Company Announces Semi-Annual Cash Dividend Of $0.88 Per Share', 'text': 'THE WALT DISNEY COMPANY ANNOUNCES SEMI-ANNUAL CASH DIVIDEND OF $0.88 PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'WEC', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'WEC Energy Group Plans to Increase Quarterly Dividend, Payable on March 1, 2020', 'text': "The board of directors of WEC Energy Group announced that it is planning to raise the quarterly dividend on the company's common stock to 63.25 cents per share in the first quarter of 2020. This would represent an increase of 4.25 cents per share. The directors expect to declare the new dividend at their regularly scheduled meeting in January. The dividend – which would be equivalent to an annual rate of $2.53 per share – would be payable March 1, 2020, to stockholders of record on February 14, 2020."}{'symbol': 'XLNX', 'date': '2019-12-05 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Analog Devices, Inc. Files Patent Infringement Lawsuit Against Xilinx, Inc', 'text': 'Analog Devices, Inc. announced that it has filed a patent infringement lawsuit against Xilinx, Inc. The lawsuit focuses on the unauthorized use by Xilinx of several important ADI patents relating to converter technology in at least two of Xilinx’s High End Zynq UltraScale + RFSoC products. The lawsuit, filed in the United States District Court for the District of Delaware, seeks damages and an injunction that prevents Xilinx from selling any products that infringe ADI’s patents.'}